P3 REUSE (depend on the component library — ADR-004; do not rebuild it)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The P3 layer already ships the shared Redis diagnostic surface — `RedisDiagnosticEmptyState`
(TeslaSync/feature-views/RedisDiagnosticEmptyState.*), the SwiftUI parity of the web
`features/admin/components/RedisDiagnosticEmptyState.tsx` that THIS page renders for
`rows.length === 0 || isError`. It owns the value type `RedisSignalsMeta` + `RedisLiveStoreMode`
(web `RedisSignalsMeta`), `RedisApiError`, and the `RedisDiagnosticModel`/`RedisDiagnosticSource`
(P1/S8). This page therefore:
  • consumes the shared `RedisSignalsMeta` / `RedisLiveStoreMode` instead of redefining them
    (an initial duplicate `RedisSignalsMeta` was removed once the build surfaced the collision);
  • composes the shared `RedisDiagnosticEmptyState` for the empty/error branch (mirrors the web page,
    and the LiveSignalInspector peer's reuse of the P3 `LiveSignalsTable`). A small adapter
    `RedisViewerDiagnosticSource` bridges the page model's resolved state into a `RedisDiagnosticInput`
    (vehicleId / meta / typed serverError vs. networkError); the "other vehicles" keys query is left
    `.idle` (chips hidden — a legitimate web state when that secondary query is pending/absent).
No P3 file was edited; this page is the intended first consumer of the (previously preview-only)
`RedisDiagnosticEmptyState` component.

