DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI RedisSignalViewerPage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure @Observable
state holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) owning the vehicles source (web useVehicles) and the cached
Redis snapshot (web getRedisSignals) over injectable seams, plus the destructive purge flow (web
purgeRedisSignals / purgeAllRedisSignals with a typed PURGE-ALL gate). The web page's six regions — the controls
GlassPanel, the four Total/Numbers/Strings/Booleans stat cards, and the signal-table GlassPanel — are rendered
with the P2 tokens + P3 shared components (TSGlassPanel/TSDataTable/TSStatCard/TSBadge/TSButton/TSToggle/
TSSearchInput/TSMaskedValue/TSSkeleton/TSEmptyState), and the empty/error branch reuses the shared P3
RedisDiagnosticEmptyState (the SwiftUI parity of the web component the page imports) — no hand-rolled diagnostic.
Every visible string resolves from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names; the page is adaptive across
macOS/iPad/iPhone and deep-linkable via the new .redisSignals route (AppRouteParser resolves /redis-signals).
Verified on BOTH idioms by isolated Swift-6 strict-concurrency type-checks (iOS view+model 0/0; the macOS full
target compiled all my files with 0 errors) and an executed model harness (34/34), with the Shared.xcframework
built GREEN. The full xcodebuild scheme is RED ONLY due to pre-existing, out-of-scope sibling defects (6 broken
*.Previews.swift + DriveScorePage.Panels.swift), with ZERO diagnostics in any of my files.

